# Files copied into a new git worktree.
#
# Worktrees are how parallel agent sessions run without colliding on one working tree.
# They start from a clean checkout, so anything gitignored is missing - which usually
# means the app does not start and the session wastes its first ten minutes on that.
#
# Local secrets ARE included here. That is the point: a worktree is on the same machine,
# under the same user, as the checkout it came from. Nothing here should ever be a
# production credential - see .claude/rules/infra.md.

.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local

# Personal, gitignored notes and overrides
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/hooks.env

# Editor and tooling state worth keeping
.vscode/settings.json
.idea/

# Expensive to rebuild, safe to share between worktrees
.certificates/
